{
  "0": "Across all four datasets, replace raw item counts in the existing frequency feature with user-balanced counts: each training interaction contributes 1/len(user_training_history). Apply the incumbent log1p, maximum normalization, square root and input attenuation 1-0.3*feature; keep unseen-item features zero. This may reduce long-history users’ influence on input suppression. Use training interactions only and store the feature in the existing checkpoint buffer. Keep embeddings, topology, readout, loss and optimizer fixed.",
  "1": "Across all four datasets, change each NextItNet block’s residual update from residual+y to residual+0.5*y. Fixed residual damping may preserve item identity through six causal convolution blocks while limiting accumulated convolution noise on short histories. Keep dilations, channels, kernels, normalization, features, embeddings, sequence selection, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer unchanged. Apply the same block definition during training and prediction, with one checkpoint per category.",
  "2": "Across all four datasets, jointly set hidden width to 48, dropout to 0.10 and learning rate to 6e-4. Width 48 previously matched incumbent macro HR@10; reduced dropout may compensate for its lower capacity, while the smaller learning rate may stabilize fitting. Preserve tied embeddings, six causal blocks, feature definitions, readout, scoring and loss. Retain seed 42, the 200-epoch cap and 200 batches per epoch; synchronize checkpoint dimensions and predictor construction.",
  "3": "Across all four datasets, replace the uniform recent-four-state mean with a causal weighted mean using weights [1,2,3,4] from oldest to current state, renormalized over nonpadding positions. Retain the 0.8 current-state/0.2 pooled-state blend. This keeps four-state context while emphasizing immediate intent, unlike the regressed two-state window. Preserve final-real-position selection, features, embeddings, backbone, scoring, loss and optimizer. Update readout metadata and the predictor writer consistently."
}
